      ⍝ Bugs28 #31 regression: selective assignment with an *empty*
      ⍝ right argument used to silently scalar-extend B's prototype
      ⍝ into every selected cell instead of raising LENGTH ERROR, the
      ⍝ way plain indexed assignment (A[...]←⍬) already correctly does
      ⍝ for the same shape mismatch -- Value::assign_cellrefs() checked
      ⍝ new_value->nz_element_count() (documented as "at least 1, for
      ⍝ the prototype"), which made a real, empty new_value look
      ⍝ exactly like a legitimate 1-element (scalar-extendable) one.
      ⍝
      A←10 20 30 40 50
      (3↑A)←⍬
LENGTH ERROR+
      (3↑A)←⍬
      ^    ^

      )SIC
      A←10 20 30
      (2↑A)←0 2⍴0
LENGTH ERROR+
      (2↑A)←0 2⍴0
      ^    ^

      ⍝ control: an each result that happens to be empty (0 0⍴⍵, not a
      ⍝ selective-assignment target) must NOT be affected -- the same
      ⍝ assign_cellrefs() is also how an *ordinary* "V←B" resolves V as
      ⍝ an lvalue (e.g. a lambda's own synthesized "λ←B"), and B←⍬ or
      ⍝ B←0 0⍴X there must always succeed regardless of B's own shape.
      ⍝
      )SIC
      ⊣{0 0⍴⍵}¨ 'a' 'b'

      ⍝ ==================================
